The legal texts come from GhaLII, the Ghana Legal Information Institute (on the Laws.Africa Peachjam platform):

  GhaLII, https://ghalii.org, point-in-time versions of each act, read from archived copies of its
  pages on the Internet Archive (https://web.archive.org), retrieved 2026-10-28.

Licence and terms, as GhaLII states them: CC BY-NC 4.0, crediting GhaLII as the source (https://ghalii.org/terms-of-use/, s. 9: "you may freely use, re-use and redistribute works from GhaLII provided you credit GhaLII as your source and your use is not for commercial gain").
CC BY-NC 4.0: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/legalcode

Attribution:

  Source: GhaLII, the Ghana Legal Information Institute (https://ghalii.org), licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial 4.0 International licence (CC BY-NC 4.0).

The texts may be used only for non-commercial purposes. This repository is private; whether and how it
may be published is the owner's decision under these terms.

Changes made by Lexifina: each version was converted to one Markdown file per provision, one paragraph per
line; spacing, quotes and dashes were normalised; editorial notes, Part and Chapter headings were left out;
and the versions were arranged as git commits credited to the laws GhaLII names for each change.
The wording of the law was not changed. Neither GhaLII nor Laws.Africa endorses this repository.

<!-- acts:start -->
Acts of Parliament in the folders acts/<year>/<number>-<short name>/: the Parliament of Ghana Library's typed editions of Acts of the
Parliament of the Republic of Ghana, from its repository (https://repository.parliament.gh/), retrieved 2026-11-03 and 2026-11-26.
The repository states no licence or terms. Under the Copyright Act, 2005 (Act 690), section 3, copyright in works
made for the Government vests in the Government. The texts are reproduced without change to their wording, as the
law of Ghana. Neither the Parliament of Ghana nor its Library endorses this repository.
<!-- acts:end -->

<!-- secondary:start -->
Executive Instruments in subsidiary/<year>/ei-<number>-<short name>/ and the Acts added from Assembly Press prints on
26 November 2026 come from the same repository (https://repository.parliament.gh/); where the print is a scan, its
text is the OCR layer that came with the PDF (no OCR was run by Lexifina). Same terms as above.

Secondary copies, used where no official copy with a usable text layer was found (each such commit carries a
Source-status: secondary copy trailer):

  WIPO Lex (https://www.wipo.int/wipolex/), the World Intellectual Property Organization's database of national laws:
  the Criminal Offences Act, 1960 (Act 29) as amended up to 2003, and the Industrial Designs Act, 2003, the
  Layout-Designs (Topographies) of Integrated Circuits Act, 2004, the Alternative Dispute Resolution Act, 2010, the
  Public Health Act, 2012 and the Plant Variety Protection Act, 2020 as passed, retrieved 2026-11-26. WIPO's terms of use:
  https://www.wipo.int/tools/en/disclaim.html. The texts are the law of Ghana (Copyright Act, 2005 (Act 690),
  section 3); WIPO does not endorse this repository.

  FAOLEX (https://www.fao.org/faolex/), the Food and Agriculture Organization's database of national laws, records
  found through ECOLEX (https://www.ecolex.org): the National Youth Authority Act, 2016, the Local Governance Act, 2016,
  the Fisheries (Amendment) Act, 2014, the Health Professions Regulatory Bodies Act, 2013 and the Economic and
  Organised Crime Act, 2010, as passed, retrieved 2026-11-26. FAO's terms (https://www.fao.org/contact-us/terms/)
  allow non-commercial reuse with credit: Source: FAOLEX, Food and Agriculture Organization of the United Nations.
  FAO does not endorse this repository.

  Office of the Special Prosecutor (https://osp.gov.gh/media/Resources/Ghana_Constitution.pdf), the Constitution of
  1992 "as Amended to 1996", and the Ghana Audit Service's copy of the 1992 text (audit.gov.gh) for the nine
  passages Act 527 of 1996 changed: government sites; no licence or terms stated.

  Used only to check the text, not copied: Constitute Project's text of the Constitution
  (https://www.constituteproject.org/constitution/Ghana_1996, CC BY-NC 3.0), and the scanned official print of the
  Constitution and of Act 527 on WIPO Lex (https://www.wipo.int/wipolex/en/legislation/details/9414).
